cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arafix in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "arafix: Evidence-Based Repair of Broken Arabic Text in Native PDFs"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21733978
abstract: >-
  arafix recovers broken Arabic text from native (non-scanned) PDFs via a
  graded repair ladder: diagnose first, then apply bidirectional reordering
  with smart LTR islands (page ranges, currencies, sentence punctuation),
  presentation-form normalization (including tatweel-in-PF protection),
  hybrid/windowed mojibake recovery (UTF-8 and legacy CP1256/ISO-8859-6),
  embedded core lexicon for ambiguous lam-alef, layout-aware extraction, and
  optional CMap repair. Core text stages are dependency-free (Python stdlib
  only). Validated on FLAW regression fixtures and a 50-package ultra-complex
  stress corpus (FPR=0, RAR=100%).
